  "title": "India extends policy to import refined palm oil at lower duty",
  "publication_date": "2022-12-29T00:00:00Z",
  "summary": "India has extended its policy allowing imports of refined palm oil at reduced duty rates and approved duty-free imports of 51,000 tonnes of cotton for 2023, according to a government notification.",
  "content": "By Rajendra Jadhav\n\nMUMBAI, Dec 29 (Reuters) - India extended a policy to import refined palm oil at a lower duty and allowed imports of 51,000 tonnes of cotton at nil duty in 2023, the government said in a notification late on Thursday.\n\nThe concession on palm oil imports comes as a relief for refiners in South Asian countries and overseas suppliers, while the duty-free cotton imports will help textile manufacturers secure supplies at lower costs.",
