  "markdown_content": "## Import Policy Updates\\n\\nMUMBAI, Dec 29 (Reuters) - India extended a policy to import refined palm oil at a lower duty and allowed imports of 51,000 tonnes of cotton at nil duty in 2023, the government said in a notification late on Thursday.\\n\\nThe concession on palm oil imports comes as a relief for refiners in South Asian countries and overseas suppliers, while the duty-free cotton imports will help textile manufacturers secure supplies at lower costs.",
